.TH IP 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ip \- configuration reseau / show and manipulate routing and devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ip
[-4] [-s] addr [show [dev X] | add A/N dev X | del A/N dev X]
.br
.B ip
link [show [X] | set X up|down [mtu N]]
.br
.B ip
route [show | add default via G [dev X] | add R/N via G | del R/N]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the SIOCGIF ioctls and /proc/net/route for display (no netlink) and runs ifconfig(8) and route(8) for changes. -s adds the counters of /proc/net/dev to
link.
.SH SEE ALSO
ifconfig(1), route(1), netstat(1)
